prison|place-of-confinement|NOUN|place where prisoners are kept|A place where people are kept as prisoners, especially as punishment after a court decision.|nhà tù; trại giam|The former prison now houses an exhibition about the island's history.|Nhà tù cũ hiện có một triển lãm về lịch sử của hòn đảo.|Countable for a building or institution; in prison and sent to prison normally omit the article when describing imprisonment.|0
toddler|young-walking-child|NOUN|young child beginning to walk|A young child who has recently begun walking.|trẻ mới biết đi|The toddler held her father's hand beside the shallow steps.|Đứa trẻ mới biết đi nắm tay bố bên cạnh những bậc thềm thấp.|Countable; toddler names a stage of development rather than a precise age that applies to every child.|-
wedding|marriage-celebration|NOUN|ceremony celebrating a marriage|A ceremony at which people marry, together with the celebrations connected with it.|lễ cưới; đám cưới|Their wedding took place in a garden behind the family house.|Đám cưới của họ diễn ra trong khu vườn phía sau ngôi nhà của gia đình.|Countable; at a wedding for attendance. Wedding names the event, while marriage also names the continuing relationship.|0
deforestation|forest-removal|NOUN|removal of forest from an area|The removal of forest trees from an area, leaving less forest there.|sự phá rừng; việc làm mất rừng|The map compares areas affected by deforestation over several decades.|Bản đồ so sánh những khu vực bị ảnh hưởng bởi nạn phá rừng qua nhiều thập kỷ.|Uncountable; deforestation of an area or caused by an activity. This names forest loss rather than ordinary pruning.|-
everything|all-things|PRONOUN|all the things in a context|All the things being considered in a particular situation.|mọi thứ; tất cả mọi việc|Everything we needed for the repair fitted into one small bag.|Mọi thứ chúng tôi cần để sửa chữa đều vừa trong một chiếc túi nhỏ.|Normally takes a singular verb; an adjective follows it, as in everything useful. The context limits what all includes.|0
